//www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> has some positive power equal to zero in <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. In a commutative ring this is equivalent to nilpotence of every finitely generated subideal of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0ALI\">Stacks 0ALI · locally nilpotent case</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/more-algebra/#tag-0ALI\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000345\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000363":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Ring homomorphisms · predicate · <code>P000363</code></p><h3>Map between Noetherian rings</h3><p>Both the source ring and the target ring are Noetherian.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07GC\">Stacks 07GC · Noetherian hypotheses</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/smoothing/#tag-07GC\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000363\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000316":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Modules · predicate · <code>P000316</code></p><h3>Maps from the module commute with filtered colimits</h3><p>For every filtered system <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathM